# s3-10 core wire (applied by CORE-WIRE-G2)

## native/core/crates/mixdog-tools/src/desktop/mod.rs
After `mod computer_ocr;` add (the trait ComputerBlobs is implemented outside this crate, so the module is public):
- `pub mod computer_pixels;`

## native/core/crates/mixdog-tools/Cargo.toml
`[dependencies]`, after `mixdog-core-api = { workspace = true }`: this crate now names `mixdog_app_protocol::v2::host::HostComputerDisplay`
(computer_pixels.rs, computer_frames.rs, computer_env.rs). It was a dev-dependency only; mixdog-app-protocol depends on
mixdog-js and mixdog-protocol only, so the edge makes no cycle.
- `mixdog-app-protocol = { workspace = true }`
Then `cargo update --workspace --offline` and `cargo hakari generate` (Cargo.lock gets the edge).

## compose_flip.rs SERVICE_PENDING
Nothing to remove: s3-10 registers no service and no protocol method.

## Compose call
None. `capture_display`, `zoom_display`, `FrameStore::assert_display_unchanged` and `desktop_bounds_env` are called by the screen capture
path of s3-18, with a `ComputerBlobs` over the core blob store (s3-18 / s3-12). Their `expect(dead_code)` attributes (module-level in
computer_pixels.rs, item-level in computer_frames.rs, computer_zoom.rs, computer_env.rs) are removed by that task when it calls them.
